-- Q4706: Financial Reporting: For-Profit [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under ASC 105-10-05 and SFAC No. 8 (OB2), the primary objective of general-purpose financial reporting is to provide information useful to existing and potential investors, lenders, and other creditors in making resource allocation decisions. This decision-usefulness objective drives all other aspects of the Conceptual Framework.
Wrong (B): Determining taxable income is governed by the IRC, not the objective of general-purpose financial reporting under GAAP.
Wrong (C): General-purpose financial statements target external users such as investors and creditors, not exclusively internal management.
Wrong (D): Calculating liquidation value relates to a specific measurement basis, not the overarching objective of financial reporting.$EXPL$
