-- Q4709: Financial Reporting: For-Profit [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under the FASB Conceptual Framework (SFAC No. 6, paragraph 82), gains are defined as increases in equity from peripheral or incidental transactions of an entity, distinct from revenues or investments by owners. A land sale outside core operations fits this definition precisely.
Wrong (A): Revenue arises from an entity''s ongoing major or central operations, not from peripheral transactions like selling surplus land.
Wrong (B): Expenses are decreases in equity from delivering goods or services in the entity''s core operations, not increases from incidental transactions.
Wrong (C): Comprehensive income is the total change in equity from non-owner sources for the period and is a broader measure, not a specific element describing peripheral gains.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 4709;

-- Q4711: Financial Reporting: For-Profit [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under ASC 105-10-05 and SFAC No. 8 (QC6-QC10), relevance means information has predictive value, confirmatory value, or both, enabling it to make a difference in the decisions made by users. Without relevance, information cannot be useful regardless of other qualities.
Wrong (A): Information that is free from error and complete describes faithful representation under ASC 105-10-05 (QC12), the other fundamental characteristic, not relevance.
Wrong (C): Information that can be independently verified describes verifiability, which is an enhancing characteristic under SFAC No. 8 (QC26).
Wrong (D): Information presented in a clear and concise manner describes understandability, another enhancing characteristic (QC30), not a fundamental one.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 4711;

-- Q4712: Financial Reporting: For-Profit [medium/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under ASC 105-10-05 and SFAC No. 8 (QC12), faithful representation requires three attributes: completeness (all necessary information is included), neutrality (free from bias), and freedom from error (no mistakes in description or process). All three must be present for a faithfully represented depiction.
Wrong (A): Predictive value, confirmatory value, and materiality are components of relevance under ASC 105-10-05 (QC6-QC11), the other fundamental characteristic.
Wrong (B): Relevance, timeliness, and comparability mix a fundamental characteristic with two enhancing characteristics and do not describe faithful representation.
Wrong (D): Verifiability, timeliness, and understandability are all enhancing qualitative characteristics, not attributes of faithful representation.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 4712;

-- Q4714: Financial Reporting: For-Profit [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under SFAC No. 8, Chapter 1, paragraph OB7 and ASC 205-40-50, the going concern assumption presumes the entity will continue in operation long enough to carry out its existing objectives and commitments. This assumption underlies historical cost accounting, systematic depreciation, and the current/noncurrent balance sheet classification.
Wrong (B): Liquidating assets within 12 months describes liquidation-basis accounting under ASC 205-30, which is the opposite of the going concern presumption.
Wrong (C): Preparing financial statements on a tax basis is a special purpose framework choice unrelated to the going concern assumption.
Wrong (D): Distributing all earnings to shareholders annually describes a dividend policy, not the going concern assumption about continuity of operations.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 4714;

